{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>and when the sun grew hot, it melted</b> — Four times in the Masorah: here; and the other: וחם הוא אבי כנען; וחם לאדני המלך; אם ישכבו שנים וחם להם. As stated in Yoma, the manna would clarify everything: if she married within three months and gave birth, uncertain whether a nine-month child of the first or a seven-month child of the last — in the house of the one whose omer was found, he was the father; and this is אם ישכבו שנים וחם להם — it would be clarified by means of וחם השמש. Likewise if he performed levirate yibbum — uncertain whether closer to him or closer to her — if her omer was found in his house, she was closer to him; and if found in her father's house, closer to her; and this is וחם לאדני המלך, which is discussed in Sanhedrin regarding levirate bonds, and וחם השמש — through it clarification would occur. Likewise regarding a Canaanite slave — this one says 'he is mine' and this one says 'he is mine' — in the house where his omer was found, he was his; and this is וחם הוא אבי כנען. Adoni Avi, the Ra'AH, of blessed memory:" "<b>and it melted</b> — Two times: here and the other: שניו יחרק ונמס. For the manna would melt and the animals would drink from it, and the nations of the world would hunt them and eat them, and would taste in them the taste of manna, and they would gnash their teeth and melt away over the good fortune of Israel:"], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {0 "The Aramaic/Hebrew term for levirate yibbum (קדושין) likely refers to the act of levirate marriage or levirate bond (קידושין); the phrase appears in the context of yibbum laws in Yoma 74b and Sanhedrin 74b. 'Adoni Avi the Ra'AH' refers to R. Aharon ha-Levi of Barcelona.", 1 "The phrase שניו יחרק ונמס appears to be from Job 16:9, where it describes an enemy gnashing his teeth — here applied to the nations who gnash their teeth in envy at Israel's good fortune."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:13:20.458289345Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}